WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.782
A CTE is useful when one stage deserves a name.

00:00:03.782 --> 00:00:07.337
It can make a multi-step query easier to read.

00:00:07.337 --> 00:00:14.022
It is especially helpful when you need to calculate a window value first and filter that result later.

00:00:14.022 --> 00:00:18.067
Recursive queries also use the CTE structure.

00:00:18.067 --> 00:00:24.472
Use a CTE because it clarifies the logic, not simply because the query is long.

00:00:24.472 --> 00:00:31.152
A CTE gives a name to an intermediate result so a complex query can be read in stages.

00:00:31.152 --> 00:00:39.387
Use it to clarify grain changes and major transformations, not simply to break every two lines into a

00:00:39.387 --> 00:00:46.320
new block. A useful CTE name describes what the rows represent, such as patient_totals or ranked_visits.
